---
import ImpactFragment from "../ImpactFragment.astro";
---

<section class="relative overflow-hidden px-[var(--gutter)] py-28 md:py-[20vh]">
  <ImpactFragment fragment="09" drift={48} driftX={28} rotate={9} class="pointer-events-none absolute -right-[5vw] top-[10%] hidden w-[17vw] text-ink opacity-[0.07] md:block" />

  <div class="relative grid grid-cols-1 gap-y-10 md:grid-cols-12 md:gap-x-10" data-reveal-group>
    <div class="md:col-span-8">
      <h2 data-reveal class="headline-editorial max-w-[10.5ch] text-[13vw] sm:text-[8.3vw] md:text-[5vw] lg:text-[4.45vw]">
        BRING US IN EARLY.
      </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="md:col-span-3 md:col-start-10 md:self-end md:pb-2">
      <p data-reveal class="body-copy">
        Bringing us in early gives the art a clear role from the start. If the direction is already defined, we can develop the work within it and carry it through production.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
